<BaseLayout title="Mods and modpacks — Ferrite docs" description="How Ferrite discovers and installs Minecraft content.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Docs / Content</div><h1>Find the right file for the right instance.</h1><p>Ferrite brings provider search, compatibility context and installation together in one workflow.</p></div></section>
  <div class="container prose"><h2>Search, inspect, install</h2><p>Browse Modrinth and CurseForge content with game-version, loader and category facets. Open a project to inspect its metadata and available versions, then install it into the selected instance.</p><h2>Loaders and formats</h2><p>Verified workflows include Fabric, Quilt, Forge, NeoForge and OptiFine, alongside mods, modpacks, resource packs, shaders and datapacks where the instance supports them.</p><h2>Provider boundaries</h2><p>Provider names are descriptive integrations. Ferrite is not affiliated with Modrinth or CurseForge, and compatibility still depends on the content publisher’s files and constraints.</p></div>
</BaseLayout>
